      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Implementing the proposed carbon emission standards will force your Ohio manufacturing plant to incur immediate and substantial infrastructure modernization costs, which could erode your competitive margin against non-compliant competitors. Operationally, stringent new regulations often disrupt established supply chains and production workflows, leading to significant unplanned downtime that threatens your ability to meet consistent client delivery schedules. Furthermore, the limited visibility and premature nature of these regulations create a high risk of \"regulatory arbitrage,\" where other states may offer tax incentives that allow your firm to shift production, effectively draining the local economy of a key industrial base.",
      "source": "target",
