      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your representative will likely argue that these regulations act as a necessary market correction to internalize the \"social cost of carbon,\" effectively predicting future market forces before they occur. They will also probably claim that strict compliance will drive \"green innovation,\" forcing the industry to adopt more efficient technologies that will ultimately lower healthcare costs from poor air quality and prevent large-scale climate disasters. However, today their insistence on innovation is still just an unproven assumption rather than a guaranteed financial outcome for you right now.",
